<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26515" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lībrātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		libro. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A making level, levelling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fortasse qui Archimedis libros legit, dicet non
					posse fieri veram ex aqua librationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					8, 6, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A horizontal position, level</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circa terrae librationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					6, 1, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A hurling off, hurling, slinging</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Diom. p. 473</span></i> P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
